## getIncomers() - React Flow

This util is used to tell you what nodes, if any, are connected to the given node as the source of an edge.

### Signature

```typescript
getIncomers(node: Node, nodes: Node[], edges: Edge[]): Node[]
```

### Parameters

| Name  | Type    | Description                                                                                                                                                                                             |
| :---- | :------ | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| node  | `Node`  | The target node to find incomers for.                                                                                                                                                                |
| nodes | `Node[]` | An array of all nodes in the React Flow graph.                                                                                                                                                       |
| edges | `Edge[]` | An array of all edges in the React Flow graph.  An edge represents a connection between two nodes.  The function will use these edges to determine which nodes are connected to the input `node`. |

### Returns

`Node[]`: An array of `Node` objects that are incomers to the given node.

### Example

```javascript
import { getIncomers } from '@xyflow/react';

const nodes = [];
const edges = [];

const incomers = getIncomers(
  { id: '1', position: { x: 0, y: 0 }, data: { label: 'node' } },
  nodes,
  edges,
);
```

